            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            has a limit, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            both
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preserved+limit"} preserves
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflected+limit"} reflects
            limits of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cone"} cone
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a limiting cone if and only if its image in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a limiting cone over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ J
          %p
            Of course, a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi F
                    %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^{op}
            creates the corresponding limit.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates all limits or colimits of a given type (i.e. over a given category
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates that sort of limit (e.g.
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates products,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates equalizers, etc.).
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          #MonadicFunctorsCreateLimits.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functors"} monadic functors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/created+limit"} create limits
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  creates all limits that exist in its
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codomain"} codomain
              %li
                %p creates all colimits that exist in its codomain and are preserved by the corresponding monad (or, equivalently, by the monadic functor itself).
            %p
          (e.g.
          = succeed ")" do
            %a{:href => "#MacLane71"} MacLane 71, Exercise IV.2.2 (p. 138)
          %p
            Creation of a particular sort of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+coequalizer"} split coequalizer
            figures prominently in Beck’s
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
          %h2#terminological_remarks Terminological remarks
          %h3#creation_of_nonexisting_limits Creation of non-existing limits
          %p It seems that the notion of “creating a limit” is used most frequently when the limits exist in the codomain. One may want to extend the terminology to cases when such limits don’t exist, which would require making a choice about whether a non-existing limit should be regarded as “created”.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories Work
            the convention is that a functor creates
            %em all
            limits that do not exist in its codomain. In this case, the more generally applicable definition could be stated as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates limits for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            has a limit whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ J
            has a limit, and
            %em in that case
            limits of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            are preserved and reflected by
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories Work
          %p
            On the other hand, one might argue that it doesn’t make sense to regard a limit that exists in the domain as being “created by the functor” if the limit in the codomain doesn’t even exist. In this case the more generally applicable definition could be stated as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates limits for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            has a limit whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ J
            has a limit, and
            %em furthermore in all cases
            limits of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            are preserved and reflected by
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %p
            Finally, one might even argue that based on the meaning of the English word “created”, only something that exists can be created at all. In this case the more generally applicable definition could be stated as “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            creates limits for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\circ J
            both have limits, and furthermore limits of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            are preserved and reflected by
            = succeed ".\u201D" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
          %h3#strictness Strictness
          %p
            The definitions given above are all “up to isomorphism”, i.e. they satisfy the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principle+of+equivalence"} principle of equivalence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Categories Work
            is additionally
            = succeed ":" do
              %em strict
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F J
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            there exists a
            %em unique
            cone
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L'
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            which is mapped
            %em exactly
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L'
            is a limit of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadicity+theorem"} monadicity theorem
            that characterizes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+algebras+for+a+monad"} category of algebras for a monad
            up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            rather than
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amnestic+functor"} amnestic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isofibrations"} isofibrations
            the strict and the non-strict notion are equivalent.
          %h2#remarks Remarks
          %p
            %a{:href => "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/punkdit/categories/26b751bbcbe6765fe447e805629ff6416f4c38b1/gmane/science/mathematics/categories/6644"} Kissinger
            suggested a concise way to state creation/preservation/etc. of limits. However, there is
            %a{:href => "https://nforum.ncatlab.org/discussion/7024/lifted-limit/?Focus=56765#Comment_56765"} some dispute
            about its correctness.
